# EventForge commit message template — Conventional Commits + Jira
#
# REQUIRED SUBJECT FORMAT:
#   <type>(<scope>): <imperative summary> [<JIRA-KEY>]
#
# Replace <JIRA-KEY> with the real Jira issue key from this project.
# EVF-123 is an EXAMPLE only; use the actual key assigned by Jira.
# Prefer <= 72 characters for the subject when practical.
# Keep the type and scope lowercase. The scope is optional.
#
# Types:
#   feat      new user-visible or architectural capability
#   fix       defect correction
#   docs      documentation-only change
#   test      tests or test fixtures
#   refactor  code restructuring without behavior changes
#   perf      measured performance improvement
#   build     build tooling or dependency changes
#   ci        continuous integration changes
#   chore     repository maintenance
#
# Suggested scopes: workflow, event-store, projections, replay,
#                   api, infrastructure, architecture, repo
#
# EXAMPLES (replace EVF-* with real Jira issue keys):
#   docs(architecture): document event-store design [EVF-1]
#   chore(repo): add Jira-aware Git templates [EVF-2]
#   feat(workflow): implement task aggregate [EVF-3]
#   fix(projections): prevent stale writes [EVF-4]
#   test(replay): cover projection rebuild [EVF-5]
#
# OPTIONAL BODY (after a blank line):
#   Why is this change needed?
#   What architectural decisions or risks matter?
#   How was it verified? (State only what was actually run.)
#
# Breaking changes must include an explanatory footer:
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <impact and required migration>
#
# The Jira key in the subject enables traceability. Automatic linking
# depends on the Jira/GitHub integration being configured.
# Avoid speculative implementation or test claims.
# Never commit confidential code, customer data, or secrets.
